# Search built-ins (B7). `A i_ndexOf B` gives the 1-origin index of each
# item of B in A (tally + 1 when absent), searching A's major cells, so
# a matrix is searched row by row. `A m_ember? B` tells for each item of
# A whether it occurs in B. Numbers compare exactly across Int and Float
# (T3); Chars with Chars (T8).
== SOURCE
5 6 7 i_ndexOf 7 9
"hello" i_ndexOf "lo"
5 6 7 i_ndexOf 6
1 2 3 i_ndexOf 2.0
(3 2 r_eshape 1 2 3 4 1 2) i_ndexOf 3 4
(3 2 r_eshape 1 2 3 4 1 2) i_ndexOf 2 2 r_eshape 1 2 9 9
2 9 m_ember? 1 2 3
"hi!" m_ember? "abcdefghi"
(2 2 r_eshape 1 5 6 2) m_ember? 1 2
== TYPE
